      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "KIP STAR (9) didn't handle the heavy going at Wagga last start after a strong start to his career on this surface. Blinkers go on for the first time today and Shaun Guymer takes the ride from a good draw. Looks well placed here on his prior form and he can strike getting back onto a firmer deck. COLD MIST (2) was competitive in similar maidens to start last campaign, beaten 1L over 1300m at Moruya early in the campaign. He was just fair in provincial grade following that, though this looks a race within his grasp on those efforts and a forward showing is expected. TEXAN STAR (5) hasn't been far away his past couple, including at this track and trip two back. Draws the inside for Loy again today and he can be in this for a long way. MONNIE (8) is better than she showed last start and won't be far away. JENNI MOO MOO (6) has claims coming back in trip.",
